<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Book of Blood</h1>
<p>The Book of Blood is the one and only way a player may take part in player 
killing (PK) on the mud. Once you are level 50 or higher, go to the library 
in Midgaard and type <a cmd='#'>sign book</a>; the book warns you, and you sign it for 
real by typing <a cmd='#'>sign book</a> again. Signing is for life: your PK flag can 
never be removed, so do not ask the Admin to remove it. Your score shows 
whether you have signed.
</p><p>Once signed, you may kill other signers, and any of them may kill you. 
Players who haven't signed can't attack you, and you can't attack them. 
When a signer dies, they are protected from player killing for about ten 
minutes, or until they quit or type <a cmd='#'>remove pk protection</a>.
</p><p>If you decide to restart the character you are on, you will NOT be 
reimbursed experience, equipment, money, quests or anything else.
</p><p>There should NEVER be an instance where a non-book of blood signer is 
PK-ed or PKing. If this happens it is considered bug abuse and grounds for 
deletion.
</p><p>Here is a list of SOME of the rules of BoB and their penalties. We 
discourage PKing in the extreme. Admin may interfere in some situations, 
such as extensive PKing of one player numerous times, or of a large number 
of players a few times.
</p>
<ul><li>A NON BoB may never PK, steal from or loot players. PENALTY: PK flagged for life.</li>
<li>A BoB may never PK, steal from or loot NON-BoB players. PENALTY: loss of 25% exp; if the player continues, deletion.</li>
<li>A NON BoB may never assist a BoB in killing, boosting stats, healing, or any other form of assistance before, during, or after a PK fight, to either party. PENALTY: PK flagged for life.</li>
<li>A NON BoB or BoB may NEVER take items from another's corpse or cause another's corpse to be lost or destroyed by any means, for example by dumping equipment to a mob or in the dump. PENALTY: inventory wipe and/or deletion.</li>
<li>NOTE: See <a cmd='#'>Help Rules</a>, as penalties can be carried across all your characters.</li>
<li>NOTE: This is a list of some of the more common problems; others are handled case by case.</li></ul>
<p>In the above named instances PK means:
</p>
<ul><li>Physically killing a player.</li>
<li>Having a mob kill a player (including summoning a player to a mob, and a mob to a player).</li>
<li>Rescuing a mob that is fighting a player who is not wanted by the law.</li>
<li>Healing a mob that is fighting a player.</li></ul>
